MT6797 MSDC1 SDR104 tuning (X20 board rework)
=============================================

This directory is the board-specific implementation of MSDC1 SD tuning,
replacing the vendor AutoK import.  The register sequence, scan counts,
latch-CK handling and failure classification follow the tuning flow that
was verified on this board; they are hardware facts of the MT6797 MSDC1
SD path and are kept, while the code is written against this board's own
register map (regs.h) and the kernel's MMIO helpers.  The vendor
multi-IP code paths this board never exercised (eMMC/SDIO AutoK, offline
tuning) are gone.  eMMC HS400 tuning lives in mtk-sd.c.

Layout:

- regs.h        MT6797 MSDC1 register offsets and fields used by tuning.
- mt6797-sd-autok.h
                Result-record layout (18 bytes) and engine entry points;
                the record is the stored replay ABI with mtk-sd.c.
- mt6797-sd-autok.c
                Tune-path setup, the two-edge command/data scans, the
                latch-CK search and result application.
- analysis.c/h  Controller-independent 64-bit window scoring and
                selection (project-original; unchanged by this rework).

mtk-sd-mt6797-autok-core.c is the mtk-sd adapter: it isolates PIO, runs
the tuning with the host IRQ off, and propagates failures to the MMC
core.  Tuning results are stored by mtk-sd.c, reapplied on clock changes
and cleared on card power-off.  Routine diagnostics are debug-only; a
failed SDR104 tuning remains an error.
